INSERT INTO [dbo].[ContentPage] ([Id], [ServiceId], [CategoryId], [Name], [Summary], [Content], [Banner], [Language], [Type], [Author], [DatePosted], [Status], [Price], [IsHome], [StartDate], [EndDate], [PortalId], [Times], [Address], [Pages], [Extentions], [FilePath], [DeliveryTime], [IsSale], [Topic], [CategoryType], [SlugType], [TimeFromTo], [Input1], [Input2], [Input3], [Input4], [Input5], [Input6], [Input8], [Input7], [Input9], [Input10], [Input11], [Input12], [IsShowHeaderContent], [Order], [NewsId], [Input13], [Input14], [Input15]) VALUES (10055, 0, 0, N'Cookie Policy', NULL, N'<p>FiinGroup Cookie Policy</p>

<p>FiinGroup sets and uses cookies and similar technologies to store and manage user preferences, deliver targeted advertising, enable content, and gather analytic and usage data, for example. The use of cookies and other tracking technologies is standard across websites and apps through which information is collected about your online activities across applications, websites, or other services. More information about how we use cookies and similar technologies and how you can control and manage them is below.</p>

<p>What is a cookie?</p>

<p>A cookie is a small text file that is placed on a computer or other device and is used to identify the user or device and to collect information. Cookies are typically assigned to one of four categories, depending on their function and intended purpose: absolutely necessary cookies, performance cookies, functional cookies, and cookies for marketing purposes.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Types of cookies and why we use them</p>

<p>Absolutely necessary cookies: These cookies are essential to enable you to move around a website and use its features. Without these cookies, Services you have asked for, like adding items to an online shopping cart, cannot be provided. Performance cookies: These cookies collect information about how you use our websites. Information collected includes, for example, the Internet browsers and operating systems used, the domain name of the website previously visited, the number of visits, average duration of visit, and pages viewed. These cookies only collect information in an aggregated format. Performance cookies are used to improve the user-friendliness of a website and enhance your experience. Functionality cookies: These cookies allow the website to remember choices you make (such as your username or ID, language preference, or the area or region you are in) and provide enhanced, more personal features. These cookies can also be used to remember changes you have made to text size, fonts, and other customizable parts of web pages. They may also be used to provide Services you have asked for, such as watching a video or commenting on a blog. These cookies cannot track your browsing activity on other websites. Targeting and advertising cookies: These cookies track browsing habits and are used to deliver targeted (interest-based) advertising. They are also used to limit the number of times you see an ad and to measure the effectiveness of advertising campaigns. They remember that you have visited a website and this information is shared with other organizations, such as advertisers.</p>

<p>Managing cookies</p>

<p>You can manage website cookies in your browser settings, and you always have the choice to change these settings by accepting, rejecting, or deleting cookies. If you choose to change your settings, you may find that certain functions and features will not work as intended on the Services. All browser settings are slightly different, so to manage cookies, you should refer to the relevant settings within your browser. We understand that you may want to know more about cookies. Here are some useful resources that provide detailed information about types of cookies, how they are used, and how you can manage your cookie preferences: www.aboutcookies.org or www.allaboutcookies.org. Please click below for detailed information on how to disable and delete cookies in some commonly used browsers:</p>

<p><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox?redirectlocale=en-US&amp;redirectslug=delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored">Mozilla Firefox&reg;</a><br />
<a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/help/17442/windows-internet-explorer-delete-manage-cookies#ie=ie-11">Microsoft&reg; Internet Explorer</a><br />
<a href="https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/61416?hl=en">Google Chrome&trade;</a><br />
<a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT201265">Safari&reg;</a></p>

<p>We use certain other tracking technologies in addition to cookies:</p>

<p>Local shared objects/Flash cookies: Flash cookies, also known as local shared objects, are designed to support browser content supported by Adobe&reg; Flash. They are usually used to enable ads and video content on websites. Like other cookies, they will store information on your device, some of which will be specific to the Flash-enabled content. Flash cookies can only be deleted within Adobe Flash rather than via your browser. Please refer to the following help page for information on how to manage your privacy settings and deletion of Flash cookies.</p>

<p>Web beacons: Our web pages may contain electronic images known as web beacons (also called single-pixel gifs and transparent graphic images) that we use to help deliver cookies on our sites, count users who have visited those sites, deliver Services, and analyze the effectiveness of our promotional campaigns, for example. We may also include web beacons in our marketing email messages or newsletters to determine whether an email is opened or if links are clicked. Web beacons are also used to deliver you interest-based advertising. Web server &amp; application logs: Our servers automatically collect certain information to help us administer and protect the Services, analyze usage, and improve users&rsquo; experience. The information collected includes:</p>

<p>&bull; IP address and browser type<br />
&bull; Device information including Unique Device Identifier (UDID), MAC address, Identifier For Advertisers (IFA), and similar identifiers we or others may assign<br />
&bull; Device operating system and other technical facts<br />
&bull; The city, state, and country from which you access our website<br />
&bull; Pages visited and content viewed, stored, and purchased<br />
&bull; Information or text entered<br />
&bull; Links and buttons clicked<br />
&bull; URLs visited before and after you use our Services</p>

<p>&ldquo;Do not track&rdquo; signals</p>

<p>Some browsers transmit Do Not Track (DNT) signals to websites. Due to the lack of a common interpretation of DNT signals throughout the industry, we do not currently alter, change, or respond to DNT requests or signals from these browsers. We continue to monitor industry activity in this area and reassess our DNT practices as necessary.</p>

<p>Connecting via social networks</p>

<p>Some of our Services may include social networking features, such as the Facebook&reg; &ldquo;Like&rdquo; button and widgets, &ldquo;Share&rdquo; buttons, and interactive mini-programs. Additionally, you may choose to use your own social networking logins from, for example, Facebook or LinkedIn&reg;, to log into some of our Services. If you choose to connect using a social networking or similar service, we may receive and store authentication information from that service to enable you to log in and other information that you may choose to share when you connect with these Services. These Services may collect information such as the web pages you visited and IP addresses, and may set cookies to enable features to function properly. We are not responsible for the security or privacy of any information collected by these third parties. You should review the privacy statements or policies applicable to the third-party services you connect to, use, or access. If you do not want your personal information shared with your social media account provider or other users of the social media service, please do not connect your social media account with your account for the Services and do not participate in social sharing on the Services.</p>
', NULL, N'en', 5, NULL, '2025-12-11 00:45:19.695', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 107, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO [dbo].[ContentPage] ([Id], [ServiceId], [CategoryId], [Name], [Summary], [Content], [Banner], [Language], [Type], [Author], [DatePosted], [Status], [Price], [IsHome], [StartDate], [EndDate], [PortalId], [Times], [Address], [Pages], [Extentions], [FilePath], [DeliveryTime], [IsSale], [Topic], [CategoryType], [SlugType], [TimeFromTo], [Input1], [Input2], [Input3], [Input4], [Input5], [Input6], [Input8], [Input7], [Input9], [Input10], [Input11], [Input12], [IsShowHeaderContent], [Order], [NewsId], [Input13], [Input14], [Input15]) VALUES (10056, 0, 0, N'Privacy Statement', NULL, N'<p>At FiinGroup, we respect your privacy. That is why we are committed to protecting your personal information. In this document, the term &quot;personal information is understood to include name, address, email address, phone number, any other personal information that you provide, or any information about you collected under current law. We hope that the document will help you understand what personal information we collect and how we use the information later. When you access and use the site (including registration and ordering products), we understand that you agree completely with the terms of this policy.</p>

<p>1. Declaration when using</p>

<p>All the contents you see on site are to serve your information needs and help you choose products. Therefore, you can use the site without providing any personal information. However, in some cases relating to downloading documents or purchasing products, we may ask you to provide personal information.</p>

<p>2. Personal information provided by you</p>

<p>When you provide necessary information, we will use them to meet your requirements; or may contact you by mail, email, text message or telephone; or, in compliance with current laws, use those vehicles to introduce to your products, services or new promotions from FiinGroup. When you provide information to us via this website, you fully understand and consent to the collection, use and disclosure of personal information for the purposes specified in this page. You fully agree and consent that the personal information you provide when using the website can be stored at the head office or branch of FiinGroup may be stored in some existing or future servers for the purpose of operating and developing the site as well as the services of FiinGroup.<br />
If you order a product, request a service or submit a response to the site, we may contact you for additional information required to process or fulfill the order and/or your request. However, we will not provide this information to a third party without your permission, except where compulsory by law or mandatory to process the order. FiinGroup is committed to protecting your privacy and not buy to sell your personal information to other companies for promotional purposes.</p>

<p>3. Providing to other entities</p>

<p>We can use some other entities to provide products or services to you. We also need to exchange your personal information to those entities to complete your request. Those entities are not allowed to use your personal information for other purposes, and we also ask them to comply with confidentiality provisions when providing services.</p>

<p>4. Collecting browser information</p>

<p>Sometimes, information can be put on your computer to help us upgrade the site and improve the quality of services to you. This information is commonly known as &quot;cookies&quot; that many web sites are currently using. &quot;Cookies&quot; are pieces of information stored on the hard disk or browser of your computer, not on the site. They allow the collection of some information about your computer such as IP address, operating system, browser type and addresses of related sites. If you do not wish to receive cookies or want to be notified when the cookies are installed, you can set your browser mode to do so if your browser supports that. Please note that, if you disable cookies, you will not be able to access or use certain features on the website, which are not predetermined. We do not intentionally limit your use in this situation; it is only the constraint in programming and building the web page.</p>

<p>5. Safety</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>When programming the site, we have set up reasonable provisions to prevent unlawful accesses and improper uses of your personal information sent to FiinGroup via the use this site. However, because there are always risks relating to providing personal data, whether directly by telephone, over the Internet or through other technical media, and there is no technical system absolutely safe against all the hackers and tampers, FiinGroup always makes precautious efforts appropriate for each information characteristics to prevent and minimize possible risks when you use this website.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>6. Information via e-mail</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>When you sign up for service, the e-mail address you provide will be used as a tool to communicate with you. First of all, please make sure that you provide that e-mail address useful to you during the service usage. We can send confidential information or receive your support request via e-mail. In case you no longer use the provided e-mail, you must inform us about the change. To protect you, FiinGroup can temporarily stop receiving requests via the e-mail you have provided if we notice of fraud or unusual information until we can contact you to confirm that.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>7. Adjusting collected information</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>FiinGroup will proactively or upon your request supplement, correct or erase inaccurate, incomplete or not updated personal information as long as you still connect with our activities.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>8. Juveniles</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>FiinGroup refuses to transact with juveniles (as regulated by local laws where you reside) without the approval of parents or legal guardians, unless local laws apply or allow.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>9. The off-site links</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>This site may contain links to other sites to introduce or supplement additional related information for your reference. FiinGroup is not responsible for the contents or actions of any other sites.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>10. Changing the terms</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>FiinGroup can change the above-mentioned terms infrequently, including supplementing, removing part of the contents or suspending the website without notice. However, if the terms are changed in ways that could be detrimental to you, FiinGroup will inform you of the change via e-mail or right on the homepage.</p>
', NULL, N'en', 5, NULL, '2025-12-11 00:46:12.212', 1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 107, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO [dbo].[ContentPage] ([Id], [ServiceId], [CategoryId], [Name], [Summary], [Content], [Banner], [Language], [Type], [Author], [DatePosted], [Status], [Price], [IsHome], [StartDate], [EndDate], [PortalId], [Times], [Address], [Pages], [Extentions], [FilePath], [DeliveryTime], [IsSale], [Topic], [CategoryType], [SlugType], [TimeFromTo], [Input1], [Input2], [Input3], [Input4], [Input5], [Input6], [Input8], [Input7], [Input9], [Input10], [Input11], [Input12], [IsShowHeaderContent], [Order], [NewsId], [Input13], [Input14], [Input15]) VALUES (10057, 0, 0, N'Terms And Conditions', NULL, N'<p>FiinGroup offers a wide range of services to build a financially credible community in Vietnam as its mission &ldquo;Enlighten the market&rdquo; and support investors and enterprises grow their businesses and gain competitive advantage. Please read the terms and conditions of this Agreement carefully. By accessing any of the Information or Services, you are acknowledging that you have read and understood the terms and conditions of this Agreement, and agree without limitation or qualification, to be legally bound by, and to comply with them. All use of FiinGroup web pages located within www.fiingroup.vn is subject to the terms and conditions set forth below (&ldquo;Terms. Any use of such web pages constitutes the user&rsquo;s agreement to abide by the Terms. We may amend the Terms at any time by posting the amended terms on this site.</p>

<p>Privacy</p>

<p>Please review our Privacy Statement, which also governs your visit to&nbsp;<a href="https://fiingroup.vn/TermsAndConditions">www.fiingroup.vn</a>&nbsp;, to understand our practices.</p>

<p>Electronic Communications</p>

<p>When you visit www.fiingroup.vn or send e-mails to us, you are communicating with us electronically. You consent to receive communications from us electronically. We will communicate with you by e-mail or by posting notices on this site. You agree that all agreements, notices, disclosures and other communications that we provide to you electronically satisfy any legal requirement that such communications be in writing.</p>

<p>Copyright</p>

<p>All content provided on this site is owned by or licensed to FiinGroup and protected by Vietnamese Regulation. FiinGroup and its licensors retain all proprietary rights to the FiinGroup Content. The FiinGroup Content may not be reproduced, transmitted or distributed without the prior written consent of FiinGroup.</p>

<p>Trademarks</p>

<p>FiinGroup logo are trademarks of FiinGroup.</p>

<p>License and Site Access</p>

<p>FiinGroup grants you a limited license to access and make personal use of this site, subject to the Terms. This site and any portion hereof may not be reproduced, duplicated, copied, downloaded, sold, resold, visited, or otherwise exploited for any commercial purpose without the express written consent of FiinGroup. You may not frame or utilize framing techniques to enclose any trademark, logo or other proprietary information (including images, text, page layout and form) of FiinGroup without the express written consent of FiinGroup. You may not use any meta tags or any other &ldquo;hidden text&rdquo; utilizing FiinGroup&rsquo; name or Marks without the express written consent of FiinGroup. Any unauthorized use terminates the license granted by FiinGroup.</p>

<p>Forward-Looking Statements</p>

<p>Certain statements included in this website are forward-looking. These forward-looking statements are based on certain assumptions and reflect our current expectations. As a result, forward-looking statements are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties that could cause actual results or events to differ materially from current expectations. There is no assurance that any forward-looking statements will materialize. You are cautioned not to place undue reliance on forward-looking statements, which reflect expectations only as of the date of this website. Except as may be required by applicable law, we disclaim any intention or obligation to update or revise any forward-looking statements.</p>

<p>Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability</p>

<p>THIS SITE IS PROVIDED BY FIINGROUP ON AN &ldquo;AS IS&rdquo; AND &ldquo;AS AVAILABLE&rdquo; BASIS. FIINGROUP MAKES NO REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, AS TO THE OPERATION OF THIS SITE, OR THE INFORMATION, CONTENT OR MATERIALS INCLUDED ON THIS SITE. YOU EXPRESSLY AGREE THAT YOUR USE OF THIS SITE IS AT YOUR SOLE RISK.<br />
<br />
